__registerContent("quickrecall/society/important-full-forms", {"notes":{"qr-important-full-forms":{"era":"Quick Recall — General Awareness","significance":["Abbreviations of key education, recruitment and examination bodies are frequent Prelims and interview quick-fire questions","Knowing the parent ministry/role of each body adds value beyond the mere expansion","These acronyms recur across governance (GS-2) and current-affairs discussions on education reform"],"features":[{"key":"Education & curriculum bodies","main":"NCERT — National Council of Educational Research and Training\nCBSE — Central Board of Secondary Education\nUGC — University Grants Commission","note":"NCERT (advisory/curriculum), CBSE (school board), UGC (higher-education regulation & grants)."},{"key":"Entrance examinations","main":"NEET — National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (medical)\nJEE — Joint Entrance Examination (engineering)\nCUET — Common University Entrance Test (university admissions)\nGATE — Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering","note":"NEET, JEE (Main) and CUET are conducted by the National Testing Agency (NTA)."},{"key":"Recruitment commissions & boards","main":"UPSC — Union Public Service Commission\nSSC — Staff Selection Commission\nRRB — Railway Recruitment Board\nIBPS — Institute of Banking Personnel Selection","note":"UPSC is a constitutional body (Articles 315–323); SSC and IBPS are for other government/bank posts."},{"key":"Defence & police services","main":"CDS — Combined Defence Services\nCAPF — Central Armed Police Forces","note":"CDS exam (by UPSC) recruits officers for the armed forces; CAPF covers forces like CRPF, BSF, CISF, ITBP, SSB."}],"traps":[{"label":"Similar-looking expansions","lines":["CBSE = Central Board of SECONDARY Education (not 'School').","NEET = National ELIGIBILITY cum Entrance Test (not 'Examination').","IBPS = Institute of Banking PERSONNEL Selection."]},{"label":"Who conducts what","lines":["UPSC conducts the Civil Services Exam and CDS/CAPF (Assistant Commandant) exams.","NTA conducts NEET, JEE (Main) and CUET.","SSC conducts exams for non-gazetted government posts."]},{"label":"Constitutional vs statutory","lines":["UPSC is a CONSTITUTIONAL body (Articles 315–323).","UGC is a STATUTORY body (UGC Act, 1956); NTA is an autonomous body under the Education Ministry."]}],"mainsAngle":"The web of examination and recruitment bodies — from UPSC and SSC to the NTA-run entrance tests — reflects both the reach of India's merit-based public recruitment and the ongoing debate over centralisation, exam integrity and equity in access to education and jobs.","mainsTheme":"Institutions of education and public recruitment in India","recall":["NCERT — National Council of Educational Research and Training","CBSE — Central Board of Secondary Education","NEET — National Eligibility cum Entrance Test","JEE — Joint Entrance Examination","UPSC — Union Public Service Commission (constitutional body)","SSC — Staff Selection Commission","RRB — Railway Recruitment Board","IBPS — Institute of Banking Personnel Selection","UGC — University Grants Commission","CUET — Common University Entrance Test","GATE — Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering","CAPF — Central Armed Police Forces","CDS — Combined Defence Services"]}},"quizzes":{"qr-important-full-forms":{"title":"Important Full Forms","questions":[{"q":"What is the correct full form of NCERT?","options":["National Centre for Educational Research and Teaching","National Council of Educational Research and Training","National Committee for Education, Research and Testing","National Curriculum and Educational Reform Team"],"correct":1,"explain":"NCERT stands for the National Council of Educational Research and Training."},{"q":"NEET stands for:","options":["National Entrance and Eligibility Test","National Eligibility cum Entrance Test","National Examination for Entry Tests","National Eligibility Evaluation Test"],"correct":1,"explain":"NEET is the National Eligibility cum Entrance Test, used for admission to medical courses."},{"q":"IBPS, associated with banking recruitment, stands for:","options":["Indian Banking and Personnel Society","Institute of Banking Personnel Selection","Indian Bureau of Public Services","Institute of Business and Personnel Studies"],"correct":1,"explain":"IBPS is the Institute of Banking Personnel Selection."},{"q":["Consider the following full forms:","I. CUET — Common University Entrance Test","II. GATE — Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering","Which of the above is/are correct?"],"options":["I only","II only","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"correct":2,"explain":"Both are correct: CUET is the Common University Entrance Test and GATE is the Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering."},{"q":"CAPF, which includes forces such as the CRPF and BSF, stands for:","options":["Central Auxiliary Police Force","Central Armed Police Forces","Combined Armed Paramilitary Forces","Central Area Protection Force"],"correct":1,"explain":"CAPF stands for Central Armed Police Forces (CRPF, BSF, CISF, ITBP, SSB, etc.)."},{"q":"Which body's full form is 'Union Public Service Commission'?","options":["SSC","UGC","UPSC","RRB"],"correct":2,"explain":"UPSC — the Union Public Service Commission — is a constitutional body that conducts the Civil Services Examination among others."},{"q":"CBSE correctly expands to:","options":["Central Board of School Education","Central Bureau of Secondary Education","Central Board of Secondary Education","Central Body for School Examinations"],"correct":2,"explain":"CBSE stands for the Central Board of Secondary Education — note 'Secondary', not 'School'."},{"q":"UGC stands for:","options":["Union Grants Council","University Grants Commission","United Graduate Council","University General Committee"],"correct":1,"explain":"UGC is the University Grants Commission, which regulates higher education and disburses grants."},{"q":"JEE, the engineering entrance examination, expands to:","options":["Junior Engineering Examination","Joint Entrance Examination","Joint Engineering Eligibility","Junior Entrance Evaluation"],"correct":1,"explain":"JEE is the Joint Entrance Examination, used for admission to engineering courses."},{"q":"SSC, which recruits for non-gazetted government posts, stands for:","options":["State Service Commission","Staff Selection Commission","Secondary Selection Council","Special Services Committee"],"correct":1,"explain":"SSC is the Staff Selection Commission, conducting exams for non-gazetted government posts."},{"q":"RRB, in the context of Indian Railways recruitment, stands for:","options":["Railway Recruitment Board","Regional Railway Bureau","Rail Reservation Board","Railway Regulatory Body"],"correct":0,"explain":"RRB is the Railway Recruitment Board."},{"q":"CDS, an exam conducted by UPSC for the armed forces, stands for:","options":["Central Defence Services","Combined Defence Services","Combined Defence Selection","Cadet Defence Scheme"],"correct":1,"explain":"CDS is the Combined Defence Services examination, conducted by UPSC to recruit officers for the armed forces."},{"q":["Consider the following full forms:","I. SSC — Staff Selection Commission","II. UGC — University Grants Commission","III. RRB — Railway Recruitment Board","How many of the above are correctly matched?"],"options":["Only one","Only two","All three","None"],"correct":2,"explain":"All three are correctly matched: SSC (Staff Selection Commission), UGC (University Grants Commission) and RRB (Railway Recruitment Board)."},{"q":"Which of the following bodies is a constitutional body?","options":["NTA","UGC","UPSC","IBPS"],"correct":2,"explain":"UPSC is a constitutional body (Articles 315–323). UGC is statutory (UGC Act, 1956) and NTA is an autonomous body."},{"q":"The entrance examinations NEET, JEE (Main) and CUET are conducted by which body?","options":["CBSE","National Testing Agency (NTA)","UGC","SSC"],"correct":1,"explain":"The National Testing Agency (NTA) conducts NEET, JEE (Main) and CUET."},{"q":["Consider the following statements:","I. UGC is a statutory body established under the UGC Act, 1956.","II. NTA is a constitutional body.","Which of the statements given above is/are correct?"],"options":["I only","II only","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"correct":0,"explain":"Only I is correct. NTA is an autonomous body under the Education Ministry, not a constitutional body."},{"q":["Match the acronym with its full form:","I. GATE — a) Common University Entrance Test","II. CUET — b) Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering","Select the correct answer:"],"options":["I-a, II-b","I-b, II-a","Both relate to engineering","Both relate to universities"],"correct":1,"explain":"GATE = Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering (b); CUET = Common University Entrance Test (a)."},{"q":"Which forces are covered under the CAPF?","options":["Army, Navy and Air Force","CRPF, BSF, CISF, ITBP and SSB","State police forces only","Territorial Army units"],"correct":1,"explain":"The Central Armed Police Forces (CAPF) include CRPF, BSF, CISF, ITBP and SSB, among others."},{"q":"The 'P' in IBPS correctly stands for:","options":["Public","Personnel","Professional","Provincial"],"correct":1,"explain":"IBPS = Institute of Banking PERSONNEL Selection — a common trap is 'Public'."},{"q":"Which body's primary role is curriculum development and educational research (advisory), rather than being a school examination board?","options":["CBSE","NCERT","UPSC","RRB"],"correct":1,"explain":"NCERT (National Council of Educational Research and Training) has an advisory/curriculum role, whereas CBSE is the school examination board."}]}}});
